---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import WrittenBy from '../components/WrittenBy.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About" description={`About ${AUTHOR}, and why this blog exists.`} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<article>
				<h1>About</h1>
				<p>
					I'm Ben Verbeken. I write software, and like everyone else I lately mostly direct agents that write it
					for me.
				</p>
				<p>
					In 2014 I co-founded <a href="https://seats.io">seats.io</a>, a seating chart and reserved
					seating platform for ticketing companies. I still spend most of my time there: designing,
					reviewing, and cleaning up after Claude.
				</p>
				<p>
					Most of this blog is about how my work is changing while it happens. Experiments,
					workflows, what works and what doesn't. Mostly for myself, partly for other developers
					going through the same thing, and a little bit for future agents.
				</p>
				<p>
					I live in Belgium with my family. Away from the keyboard I sing in <a
						href="https://captainsugar.be/">Captain Sugar &amp; The Daddies</a
					> and go <a href="https://www.strava.com/athletes/63708615">running</a>. Sometimes I write about that too.
				</p>
				<h2>How I use AI</h2>
				<p>
					I use AI for writing. Sometimes a lot, sometimes not at all.
					I don't think there's anything wrong with that, but I do think it's important to be transparent about it.
				</p>
				<p>
					So I label each post with how much AI I used:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><WrittenBy by="human" /> <strong>Human-written</strong>: I built the structure and wrote the text. AI only proofread it, for example to find typos.</li>
					<li><WrittenBy by="assisted" /> <strong>AI-assisted</strong>: the ideas, structure and choices were mine, and I wrote most of the text or reworked it. AI may have put together a first draft from an interview with me, or improved the wording.</li>
					<li><WrittenBy by="ai" /> <strong>AI-written</strong>: AI wrote the text from start to finish, and I only made a few edits.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Whatever the label, the ideas and experiences are mine. AI helps me put them into words, not come up with them.
				</p>
				<p>
					More on this in <a href="/blog/writing-with-ai/">Writing with AI</a>.
				</p>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
<style>
	li :global(.written-by) {
		color: var(--accent);
	}
</style>
